Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Cascade Spectra", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.6385392196837587`*^9, 3.638539227770125*^9}, {
  3.656975727748878*^9, 
  3.656975727875676*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"00cf4803-6d60-4869-b01e-\
89be371165d2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
This file describes the contents of the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Spectra\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] directory and further below examples of how to load \
them into Mathematica\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.639076207803432*^9, 3.6390762404838963`*^9}, 
   3.639076317436984*^9, {3.6390765046563883`*^9, 3.639076514397648*^9}, {
   3.644586340142351*^9, 3.644586353618786*^9}, 3.644586384418253*^9, {
   3.644586441815485*^9, 3.644586484755768*^9}, {3.6445972985754833`*^9, 
   3.6445972995183773`*^9}, {3.6569757500214376`*^9, 3.65697575353046*^9}, {
   3.656975998022893*^9, 
   3.656975999366453*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fa2c62c4-e5f0-4ba2-9772-\
0f700fb30a77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Supplementary material for G. Elor, N. Rodd, T. Slatyer, W. Xue, \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Model-Independent Indirect Detection Constraints on \
Hidden Sector Dark Matter\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (2015)",
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Contact: Nick Rodd <nrodd@mit.edu>\n\nUpdated in January 2018 to include \
neutrino final states."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.644586317093876*^9, 3.644586336763632*^9}, 
   3.657207983037204*^9, {3.726157087112405*^9, 
   3.7261570994886103`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8a9520e0-c165-4356-877c-\
86c5b3e176cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Overview: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Files within \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Spectra\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] contain \
the \[Gamma], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["e", "+"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", "-"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c57bf32d-aeb6-413c-a4ae-3774bfffa9df"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["p", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "962942fc-312e-4103-be53-fa540892af78"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Nu]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"e", "/", "\[Mu]"}], "/", "\[Tau]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "5ec8ee8a-712c-4043-afea-21e8f067a1fd"],
 " spectrum of dark matter (DM) annihilations leading to 1-6 step cascades \
ending in ",
 StyleBox["e",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", \[Mu], \[Tau], ",
 StyleBox["b",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "-quark, ",
 StyleBox["W",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["H",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " or gluon final states. A separate .dat file is provided for each type of \
spectrum and final state. Note all spectra here are calculated using the \
large hierarchy approximation, which can break down in certain situations. \
The contents of these files are designed to be similar to the results of M. \
Cirelli et al., JCAP ",
 StyleBox["1103,",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " 051 (2011), 1012.4515.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["version details:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " this file was written in Mathematica 10. It runs fine (but with some \
harmless error messages) in Mathematica 9. Due to the use of the PlotLegends \
function, it will not operate with Mathematica 8, but if these are deleted \
the files will run.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Content of files:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " There are 18 files of the form Cascade_{Final State}_{Spectrum Type}.dat. \
Each contains 8 columns and 1612 rows (the first row contains the column \
labels and all others contain numerical values). For all files ",
 StyleBox["except",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " gluon final states and the positron spectrum from gammas, the columns are: \
\n1. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "544b6e16-86ba-40ab-abee-2e00736f5e9b"],
 " value; \n2. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["Log", "10"], "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"c4973936-8b1a-4d9f-87b3-6bcfc26f5863"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "=", 
    RowBox[{"E", "/", 
     SubscriptBox["m", "DM"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ebd7efc9-3bcf-4ea9-9eb8-59c831deb4e9"],
 "; \n3-8. the value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["dN", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["dLog", "10"], "(", "x", ")"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ln", "(", "10", ")"}], "x", " ", 
     FractionBox["dN", "dx"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "75714df0-0c04-4c53-a2ee-0e368e4063ee"],
 " of an n=1 (column 3) up to n=6 (column 8) spectrum at that value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "14c996dc-b363-4aa1-ae6f-d43b96839c43"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e720046f-a7ce-4bb4-9674-a04797cc689b"],
 ". \nFor final state gluons and the positron spectrum from gammas, the \
columns are:\n1. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "52329404-11a5-436e-a9f8-f61a11ce8c53"],
 " value; \n2. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["Log", "10"], "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"37fca38e-4ad6-4fac-9fd5-4dd630eb450b"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"x", "=", 
    RowBox[{"E", "/", 
     SubscriptBox["m", "DM"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7f534db7-0dd0-4351-ab0e-fb739c6df21c"],
 "; \n3-8. the value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["dN", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["dLog", "10"], "(", "x", ")"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ln", "(", "10", ")"}], "x", " ", 
     FractionBox["dN", "dx"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "66f2491d-3fe8-4dbb-84ac-02911c94a60b"],
 " of an n=1 (column 3) up to n=6 (column 8) spectrum at that value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d71cac55-7c8e-432d-82bb-f315388c0fc4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ae3755ee-ff9c-416c-ba50-f609ec183b27"],
 ". \nThe reason for this difference in the case of gluons and the positron \
spectrum from gammas is that we have to use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b6ab9190-dc14-426e-a77f-670ad61dbfa3"],
 " values instead of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["m", "f"], "/", 
      SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ea7bce54-8eaf-4685-a546-f528b65b4411"],
 " as for these final states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["m", "f"], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7c066a76-7c60-4935-b75b-feedd52f24de"],
 " making ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e87019d2-b6fe-4e74-8abd-e585db58f4e7"],
 " less useful.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Range of parameters: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["Log", "10"], "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"0bdec07d-0581-4da5-a89e-126a48d421b5"],
 " ranges from -8.9 to 0 in steps on 0.05, covering the entire range where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], 
    RowBox[{"dN", "/", "dx"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6375cd6e-43cb-41ca-8b42-7844568a471f"],
 " for each spectra is non-zero. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9b3bacde-2d7b-4649-9ae4-d57da365ec47"],
 " is evaluated at 0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.07, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4 and 0.5, whilst \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aedd1b8a-bf52-486d-a28d-27df69ddccac"],
 " is given at 10, 20, 40, 50, 80, 100, 500, 1000 and 2000 GeV.\n",
 StyleBox["NB:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " if using a value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Epsilon]", "f"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1beecf2c-8d73-4230-a99b-102f0ee505b2"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "74e4e4ea-c79f-4796-807b-dd9d117f500c"],
 " not in this list - especially if it is outside the range of values \
provided - it is recommended that linear interpolation be used, as described \
in the examples below.\n",
 StyleBox["NB:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " as we are using an interpolating function to determine the spectrum, it \
can occasionally go negative. This is unphysical can cause issues if the Log \
of the spectrum is being used, and so we set the spectrum to 0 wherever the \
interpolating function would send it negative.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Brief description of files",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Photon Spectra:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nCascade_{Gam,E,Mu,Tau,B,W,H,G}_gammas.dat - photon spectrum from final \
state {photons, electrons, muons, taus, b-quarks, Ws, Huggs, gluons}\n\n",
 StyleBox["Positron/Electron Spectra:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nCascade_{Gam,E,Mu,Tau,B,W,H,G}_positrons.dat - positron (or equivalently \
electron) spectrum from final state {photons, electrons, muons, taus, \
b-quarks, Ws, Huggs, gluons}\n\n",
 StyleBox["Antiproton Spectra:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nCascade_{B,W,H,G}_antiprotons.dat - antiproton spectrum from final state \
{b-quarks, Ws, Higgs, gluons}\n",
 StyleBox["NB:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " electron, muon and tau antiproton spectra are negligible and so not given\n\
\n",
 StyleBox["Nue and Numu spectrum",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nCascade_{Nu,Mu,Tau,B,W,H,G}_{nue,numu}.dat - nue/numu spectrum from final \
state {nue/numu, muons, taus, b-quarks, Ws, Huggs, gluons}. \n",
 StyleBox["NB:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t include electrons as these \
don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t decay to neutrinos\n\n",
 StyleBox["Nutau spectrum",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nCascade_{Nu,Tau,B,W,H}_nutau.dat - nutau spectrum from final state \
{nutau, muons, taus, b-quarks, Ws, Huggs, gluons}.\n",
 StyleBox["NB: ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t include muons or gluons as these don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t produce tau neutrinos in any appreciable amount.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Direct Spectra:",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nAtProduction_{gammas,positrons,antiprotons,neutrinos_e,neutrinos_mu,\
neutrinos_tau}.dat",
 StyleBox[" -",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " Direct {photon, positron, antiproton, nue, numu, nutau} spectrum as \
calculated by M. Cirelli et al. These files were produced by those authors, \
but we provide them here for convenience."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJwd0W8w0wEcBvCdk1CSmltjbMNpmvythSn3Q9yR/rjrumqVMRPtxsSZXeZO
q5P+uLOuF71YXF1Co3FK0Y6bliFC6OaSS5c0l/IGa6nf83vxvc+L5557Xny5
